WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.875
- He cut the legs off the
jockstrap, so he would just—

00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:04.792
- Wait, you wore a jockstrap?

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:08.625
- The best "Box 'Em Up" story
happened to Brian Urlacher.

00:00:08.625 --> 00:00:11.042
- Ohhh my God.

00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:15.708
♪♪♪

00:00:15.708 --> 00:00:21.667
- ♪ Never mind,
I'll find someone like Hue ♪

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:26.042
♪ We wish nothing
but the best ♪

00:00:26.042 --> 00:00:27.542
♪ for you ♪
- [Fake sobbing]

00:00:27.542 --> 00:00:31.083
How did this happen?

00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:32.708
- I mean, what?!
"How did it happen?"

00:00:32.708 --> 00:00:34.958
Are you kidding me?
He's 3-36-1.

00:00:34.958 --> 00:00:36.792
- I love it.
- That's how it happened.

00:00:36.792 --> 00:00:38.583
- I need
to remind people

00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:43.292
Bill Belichick would need
to lose 1,070 games in a row

00:00:43.292 --> 00:00:45.875
to have a worse winning
percentage than Hue Jackson.

00:00:45.875 --> 00:00:47.708
- That's a great stat.
Good job on that one.

00:00:47.708 --> 00:00:49.500
- That's insane.
- Yeah, I like that.
- I mean, it's from Reddit.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.208
- It's insane.
- Yes.
- But it's still insane.

00:00:51.208 --> 00:00:53.000
- Welcome to "Simms &amp; Lefkoe."

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:54.583
That was the news
of the weekend

00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:56.667
but there's a lotta stuff
goin' on this week

00:00:56.667 --> 00:01:00.292
and it is time
for midseason awards.

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:06.000
For our midseason awards,
we're not doing

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.625
[Robotic voice] MVP—
- At the halfway point

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.833
- Offensive Player of the Year, meh.
No, we have our own style

00:01:10.833 --> 00:01:14.708
and first, we're doin'
Best Player No One's Talking
About in the First Half.

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:16.375
Who you going with?
- I'm gonna go with Cam Newton.

00:01:16.375 --> 00:01:18.792
I mean, he's the quarterback
of a 5-2 football team.

00:01:18.792 --> 00:01:20.208
- True.
- OK?

00:01:20.208 --> 00:01:21.792
He does not get the respect
he deserves

00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:24.208
because he doesn't throw
for 400 yards

00:01:24.208 --> 00:01:27.583
and five touchdowns every week,
but I will say this

00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:31.500
Trying to defend him can't be
quantified sometimes, Lefkoe.
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.083
- You know you like that word.
- That is the Worst Phrase
of the First Half of the Season.

00:01:34.083 --> 00:01:35.875
I am gonna go deeper cut.
- Yes.

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:38.542
- I'm going Frank Clark
of the Seattle Seahawks.
- OK.

00:01:38.542 --> 00:01:40.167
One of the league leaders
in sacks

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:42.292
and every time
I watch the Seahawks game

00:01:42.292 --> 00:01:44.917
the quarterback is running
for his life from Frank Clark.
- Yep.

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:47.333
I mean, Cam's—I mean,
nobody gives Cam respect.

00:01:47.333 --> 00:01:50.625
- All right, next up,
Good, Bad, Good Award

00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:52.708
People that were good,
then they were bad,
then they were good.

00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:55.500
I believe this should be called
the Ryan Fitzpatrick Award.
- Right.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.167
- I am giving it
to Ryan Fitzpatrick.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:58.625
- OK.
- It is synonymous with

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:01.125
not just his career
but also this season.
- Yes it is.

00:02:01.125 --> 00:02:03.000
- He was incredible,
and then he disappeared

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.875
and then he's back again,
and it's amazing.

00:02:04.875 --> 00:02:06.417
Who you goin' with?
- I'm gonna go with Dee Ford

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:07.958
on the Kansas City Chiefs.
- Ooh, deep cut.

00:02:07.958 --> 00:02:09.750
- He was a first-round
pick, OK.

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.625
Kinda had a decent start
to his career

00:02:11.625 --> 00:02:13.708
then everybody's like,
"Who is this guy?
He's horrible!"

00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:15.500
He became an Internet meme.
- Yes.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:17.125
- And now he's the best player
on the Kansas City defense.

00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:18.458
- I like that one.

00:02:18.458 --> 00:02:21.042
- All right, so everyone's gonna
focus on Coach of the Year.

00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:23.583
We know that the real money
is made with coordinators.

00:02:23.583 --> 00:02:25.292
- Right.
- Which coordinator do you wanna

00:02:25.292 --> 00:02:27.375
give shine as Best
Coordinator in the First Half?

00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:29.125
- Greg Manusky,
defensive coordinator

00:02:29.125 --> 00:02:30.250
for the Washington Redskins.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.917
No. 4 defense in football.

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.667
And all anybody remembers
about the year

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.583
is the Monday night game against
Drew Brees after a bye week.

00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:38.042
Yeah, they laid
an egg that week

00:02:38.042 --> 00:02:39.708
but other than that,
they've been phenomenal

00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:41.583
and there's not a lotta
superstars on that defense.

00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:43.125
- And they're No. 2
against rushing—
- There you go.

00:02:43.125 --> 00:02:44.542
- Which is pretty amazing.
- Right.

00:02:44.542 --> 00:02:46.625
- I have to give an apology
and an award.

00:02:46.625 --> 00:02:49.708
Norv Turner, I am sorry
I made fun of you

00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:51.292
this offseason
and said you had hired

00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:53.917
your entire family tree
for your coaching staff

00:02:53.917 --> 00:02:56.375
and that you quit on Mike Zimmer
in Minnesota.

00:02:56.375 --> 00:02:58.000
And you've proven me wrong, sir.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.542
- Way to self-scout yourself.
- 5-2, Carolina Panthers.

00:03:00.542 --> 00:03:03.333
Cam Newton, this offense:
little bit of this,
little bit of that.

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:06.250
- Yep.
- Little bit of apology.
I'm sorry, Norv. You're the man.

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:10.625
Now the most important award
for our midseason extravaganza!

00:03:10.625 --> 00:03:14.375
The Best Player that
People Think Simms Hates.

00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:17.167
- Oh, OK. Jared Goff.
That would be the guy
that I think has had——

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.875
- People definitely think
you hate Jared.

00:03:18.875 --> 00:03:20.667
- Yeah, they really do,
and I'll say, you know

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:23.042
I definitely was skeptical
about him coming into the year

00:03:23.042 --> 00:03:25.917
but again, it's the plays
he makes that aren't there

00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:27.833
that I think are
extremely impressive.

00:03:27.833 --> 00:03:29.792
Scrambling,
people around the pocket

00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:31.875
big throws down the field.
- Yes.
- He deserves credit.

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:34.167
- I think the player
that people think you hate

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.458
that's playing the best is Matt Ryan.
- He's been ballin'.

00:03:36.458 --> 00:03:38.958
- And I would say it's been a
year-and-a-half of Matt Ryan

00:03:38.958 --> 00:03:42.042
playin' the best football
of his career.
- Right.

00:03:42.042 --> 00:03:44.292
- And it's—the team carried him
early in his career.

00:03:44.292 --> 00:03:46.500
He's carrying the team
right now.
- Agree with that.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.583
- And you don't hate Matt Ryan.

00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.208
- I don't hate Matt Ryan at all.
- Good.

00:03:49.208 --> 00:03:51.292
You know who else you don't hate?
- What?
- Brian Urlacher.

00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:53.000
- Ooh, I like Urlacher.
- But you know
what Brian Urlacher hated?

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.917
- What?
- Being put into a box.

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:57.708
- Put into a box? Well, who
would like to be in a box?

00:03:57.708 --> 00:04:00.250
- Apparently, the Chicago Bears.

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:04.417
- The best Box 'Em Up story
happened to Brian Urlacher.

00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:08.417
- I can't believe you got him.
- The best. The greatest one.

00:04:08.417 --> 00:04:10.417
We created this game
that was called Box 'Em Up

00:04:10.417 --> 00:04:13.042
because everybody got,
like, Nike and Reebok shoes

00:04:13.042 --> 00:04:14.917
and different things
and clothes

00:04:14.917 --> 00:04:16.875
and then you'd have the boxes,
the cardboard boxes left over.

00:04:16.875 --> 00:04:19.292
So people would be walkin', and
if they're not payin' attention

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:21.667
you just run up behind 'em
and slam a box over their head

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:23.083
and say, "Box 'em up!"

00:04:23.083 --> 00:04:24.542
So everybody had to have

00:04:24.542 --> 00:04:26.417
their head on a swivel
in the locker room.

00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:28.083
So Brian was really good

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:29.917
at getting other people, too,
cuz he's sneaky.

00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:32.125
Like, he'd get you comin' out of
your meeting room or something

00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:34.708
and, boom, you got a box
slammed over your head.

00:04:34.708 --> 00:04:36.583
He would get so many people
that, yeah

00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:38.375
everybody kinda
had it out for him.

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:40.500
- Everybody turned on him.
He was the box bully.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.667
- Yeah. It only took me once.
You get boxed on once—

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.250
- You got the head
on a swivel.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.083
- Like, literally,
around the locker room

00:04:46.083 --> 00:04:47.917
you got your back to the wall.
- [Laughing]

00:04:47.917 --> 00:04:50.292
- I'm keepin' everybody
in front of me.

00:04:50.292 --> 00:04:52.292
I think the D-line
brainstormed on, like

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:54.500
"What would be the best way
to try to get him?"

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:56.208
And, I mean, it was brilliant.

00:04:56.208 --> 00:04:58.833
- I'm imaging the D-line
doing, like, a space shuttle launch.

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:02.125
- Yeah, they probably had,
like protractors and
all kind of stuff.

00:05:02.125 --> 00:05:03.708
You know, it's Urlacher,
so you gotta get him.

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:05.208
- Yes, right.
- I don't know

00:05:05.208 --> 00:05:07.667
how they got this box, but
it was like a six-foot box.

00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:11.292
And in our locker room, there's
stairs to go to the second floor

00:05:11.292 --> 00:05:13.000
where all the cardio stuff is

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.167
and there's a platform,
so you can't see who's up there.

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.833
So he comes out, and so right when

00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:19.333
he walks out from
under the platform

00:05:19.333 --> 00:05:22.125
somebody drops that six-foot box
right on his head.

00:05:22.125 --> 00:05:24.333
He had his arms down.
It dropped, like,
straight over him.

00:05:24.333 --> 00:05:26.750
He's like, "Ahhh! Ahhh!
I'm stuck in the box!"

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:28.833
And he's, like, trying
to get it off of him.

00:05:28.833 --> 00:05:30.500
Everybody's like,
"Box 'em up!"

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:31.958
All you saw was
two little feet, like

00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:34.333
kickin' out of the box
and stuff.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:37.000
- [Laughing]
- That's awesome.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.792
This is a special moment for me.

00:05:38.792 --> 00:05:40.833
This is somebody that I love—
- Oh my gosh.

00:05:40.833 --> 00:05:42.958
- With all of my heart,
Brian Westbrook!

00:05:42.958 --> 00:05:44.583
- Dude, don't give him
your cellphone number.
- [Laughing]

00:05:44.583 --> 00:05:46.333
- I'll text you all the time.

00:05:46.333 --> 00:05:50.042
- Stage 9 clinger over here.
Don't do it.
- Love it, love it.

00:05:50.042 --> 00:05:52.375
- All right, chill.
- Stalker alert!
- We just heard Matt Forte talk about pranks.

00:05:52.375 --> 00:05:55.917
Eagles locker room:
you, Trot, T.O., McNabb

00:05:55.917 --> 00:05:57.708
Freddie Mitchell,
all those guys.

00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:59.583
Any pranks come to mind
right away?

00:05:59.583 --> 00:06:02.000
- You named him—
Freddie Mitchell, always.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.875
I'm not sure
that he ever practiced

00:06:03.875 --> 00:06:08.042
or did anything with meetings,
but he loved pranks.

00:06:08.042 --> 00:06:09.792
And this is a small one.

00:06:09.792 --> 00:06:11.708
So, you go and you put your
jockstrap on, ready to play.

00:06:11.708 --> 00:06:13.542
- Yeah.
- He'd cut the legs

00:06:13.542 --> 00:06:15.125
off the jockstrap,
so you just—

00:06:15.125 --> 00:06:17.542
- Just have that part.
- Just hanging.

00:06:17.542 --> 00:06:19.042
But that wasn't the worst one.

00:06:19.042 --> 00:06:20.667
- Wait, you wore a jockstrap?

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:22.708
I just wore spandex.
- Really?

00:06:22.708 --> 00:06:24.667
- He believes no NFL players
wear cups.

00:06:24.667 --> 00:06:26.000
- Well, not a cup—
- He knows they don't wear cups.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.667
- But the jockstrap.
- I didn't know.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:30.417
- I needed to be held in there,
secure. Yeah, of course.

00:06:30.417 --> 00:06:31.958
- All right.
Just wanted to clear that up, OK.

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:34.167
- We're all secure here
in our manhood. Trust me.

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.042
[Laughing]

00:06:36.042 --> 00:06:38.792
The other thing is, he was on
the Bucs, his spleen explodes—

00:06:38.792 --> 00:06:40.625
Sorry for bringing it up.
- Yeah, it's all right.

00:06:40.625 --> 00:06:43.042
- And, like, a few games later,
you guys go down to Tampa Bay

00:06:43.042 --> 00:06:44.833
and you had one of
the greatest plays

00:06:44.833 --> 00:06:46.833
I've ever seen
that no one will remember.

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:48.750
- We were up by about 20 points.
- You were up big, yeah.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.500
- Furious comeback

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.208
and that was my first experience
seein' this guy right here.

00:06:52.208 --> 00:06:55.833
- Little dump-off, like 50,
60 yards. You weaved in and out.

00:06:55.833 --> 00:06:57.458
Break a couple ankles,
make some guys miss.

00:06:57.458 --> 00:06:58.958
I'm kinda struttin'
to the end zone.

00:06:58.958 --> 00:07:00.458
It's only a minute left.

00:07:00.458 --> 00:07:02.417
There's no way, no way,
Tampa Bay's gonna

00:07:02.417 --> 00:07:04.750
kick the return and return it.
- Right.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:07.167
- Bruce Gradkowski.
- The starting quarterback's
not in there.

00:07:07.167 --> 00:07:08.750
Simms is in there,
so there's no way.

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:11.042
- Exactly, exactly.
- And then Matt Bryant

00:07:11.042 --> 00:07:14.167
kicked that 62-yard field goal
for the Bucs.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.833
So you were filled with joy.
He was filled with pain.

00:07:16.833 --> 00:07:18.333
- I was first filled
with amazement.

00:07:18.333 --> 00:07:20.292
It was my first time that
I was on a field with him

00:07:20.292 --> 00:07:22.125
and got to see him pull
some of these plays off

00:07:22.125 --> 00:07:23.542
that he did
in the fourth quarter.

00:07:23.542 --> 00:07:26.042
- Yeah.
- And he's ahead of his time

00:07:26.042 --> 00:07:27.708
at that position.
- I agree.

00:07:27.708 --> 00:07:29.542
- You know, now I feel like
there's a lot of guys—
- Lot of 'em.

00:07:29.542 --> 00:07:31.208
- Like you around the NFL,
and that's the first place—

00:07:31.208 --> 00:07:33.083
Like, who's the guy
you look at in the NFL

00:07:33.083 --> 00:07:35.083
right now that you're amazed by

00:07:35.083 --> 00:07:37.875
or reminds you of you
at running back?

00:07:37.875 --> 00:07:40.875
- It's a couple guys.
I mean, Jerick McKinnon—

00:07:40.875 --> 00:07:43.333
they were gonna use him—
- Yes.

00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:45.292
- The same way that they used me.
Obviously, he gets injured.

00:07:45.292 --> 00:07:48.542
Tarik Cohen, this last month of the season—
- That's the mensch! That's our guy.

00:07:48.542 --> 00:07:50.708
- They continue to use him
more and more.

00:07:50.708 --> 00:07:54.042
James White, Dion Lewis,
same type of guy.

00:07:54.042 --> 00:07:57.458
- Something happened on Sunday.
I thought of you immediately.

00:07:57.458 --> 00:07:58.708
- What’s that?

00:07:58.708 --> 00:08:02.667
- Todd Gurley takes the ball,
runs down, slides right there

00:08:02.667 --> 00:08:06.458
on the 1-yard line, no touchdown.
Fantasy players are going nuts,

00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:09.417
Vegas is going crazy.
You did that to Dallas. 

00:08:09.417 --> 00:08:13.208
You know, I– of course I admire what 
Todd Gurley continues to do week in

00:08:13.208 --> 00:08:17.292
and week out, and having done
that against the Cowboys years ago,

00:08:17.292 --> 00:08:20.250
I wish he would have scored.
I’m all about fantasy now.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.083
When I was playing,
it wasn’t about fantasy, nothing.

00:08:23.083 --> 00:08:26.792
Now I’m all like, listen, score as much
as you can, as often as you can.

00:08:26.792 --> 00:08:27.917
I need it for my team.

00:08:27.917 --> 00:08:30.875
- That’s nonsense. I was up against Gurley
and I was like, “you sit down and don’t

00:08:30.875 --> 00:08:31.958
 get in that end zone!”
- Exactly. You loved it, right.

00:08:31.958 --> 00:08:34.875
- Pose the point that if they score the
touchdown and maybe miss the

00:08:34.875 --> 00:08:37.417
extra point, which we see all the time–
-Yeah.

00:08:37.417 --> 00:08:40.500
- It’s gonna be an 8-point lead and you’re still
gonna give Aaron Rodgers the ball back.

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:41.542
- That’s true.

00:08:41.542 --> 00:08:43.958
- So did you wanna play with that kind of fire?
I wouldn’t have.

00:08:43.958 --> 00:08:46.625
- In hindsight, now retired, and not having
to worry about the team winning–

00:08:46.625 --> 00:08:48.167
- Cuz you got so much praise for it back then.

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:51.875
I know, people love it. Especially
people in Philly, they loved the play.

00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:53.667
Everywhere else, they’re like,
“what are you doing?”

00:08:53.667 --> 00:08:55.125
- I was gonna go to Andy Reid.

00:08:55.125 --> 00:08:56.458
- That's exactly
where I wanna go too.

00:08:56.458 --> 00:08:57.958
Just what he's doin' there.

00:08:57.958 --> 00:08:59.958
- He's got a one-loss team
with Patrick Mahomes.

00:08:59.958 --> 00:09:02.125
Do you have joy
watching this happen?

00:09:02.125 --> 00:09:03.583
- I have so much joy.

00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:06.208
I mean, I love Andy
as a coach, as a man.

00:09:06.208 --> 00:09:08.125
Certainly a guy that
I looked up to

00:09:08.125 --> 00:09:10.542
and appreciate everything
he did for my career.

00:09:10.542 --> 00:09:12.708
Quick story:
When we got Mike Vick

00:09:12.708 --> 00:09:14.750
I talked to Andy,
and he was like

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:18.250
"I've been drawing up plays
on napkins for Vick

